WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
In the early Chu–Han contention, Liu Bang's forces were trapped in Hanzhong, with high mountains on every side.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.102
To return to Guanzhong, they had to find a clever way.

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:12.724
Han Xin offered a brilliant plan: openly send men to repair the plank roads, to mislead the enemy.

00:00:13.074 --> 00:00:16.626
Hearing this, Liu Bang's eyes lit up, and he nodded his agreement to the plan.

00:00:16.976 --> 00:00:22.208
The plank-road workers hammered away, the sound carrying far — and Xiang Yu's scouts all saw it.

00:00:22.558 --> 00:00:26.326
The enemy scouts saw it and truly believed the Han army would attack along the plank road.

00:00:26.676 --> 00:00:30.444
The workers sang as they worked, pretending to repair the road slowly, in no hurry at all.

00:00:30.794 --> 00:00:36.266
But in secret, the main Han force quietly set out along the Chencang path, heading straight for Guanzhong.

00:00:36.616 --> 00:00:41.656
The mountain path was narrow and dangerous; the soldiers led their horses and advanced with great care.

00:00:42.006 --> 00:00:50.214
By the time Xiang Yu realized it, the Han army had already taken Guanzhong. 'Repair the roads openly, advance secretly through Chencang' became a famous stratagem for the ages.

00:00:50.564 --> 00:00:54.524
This story teaches us to be flexible — and to catch others by surprise.

